hymeko-optimize <model.hymeko> [options]

  --backend rust|external   in-process augmented Lagrangian, or a child process (default: rust)
  --python <exe>            interpreter for the external backend (default: $HYMEKO_PYTHON or python)
  --script <path>           driver for the external backend (default: backends/slsqp.py)
  --multistart <n>          try n deterministic starting points and keep the best (default: 1)
  --out <file.json>         write the result as evidence
  --quiet                   only the exit status

The model is the only place the design is written. There is no flag for a target, a bound, or a
scenario: those are declarations, and a command line that could override them would be a second
place to edit them.

Exit status is 0 when a feasible design was found and its constraints hold.
